upstream tracker reference in docs/api/core/network.md:339:  - `PerformanceInterceptor` sits after `AuthInterceptor` and `RetryInterceptor` so each trace records how the request finally ended. A 401 that is refreshed and replayed is resolved from `AuthInterceptor.onError`, which in dio ends the host chain - so the 401 replay client borrows the host's `ApiLoggingInterceptor` and `PerformanceInterceptor`, and the replay carries the original request's `extra` (and with it the trace). One trace covers the refreshed request and records the replay's 200; a retried request keeps its trace too (koniz-dev/flutter-starter#298, #477).
